      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\n`RocmPlatform.use_custom_allreduce()` returns true only for gfx94x and gfx95x. On gfx1250, vLLM therefore sets `disable_custom_all_reduce=True`, and every tensor-parallel all-reduce goes through RCCL. This PR adds gfx1250 to the list, so gfx1250 uses AITER's custom allreduce the same way MI300/MI350 do.\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n-        # We only enable custom allreduce for MI300 series\r\n-        return any(gfx in _GCN_ARCH for gfx in [\"gfx94\", \"gfx95\"])\r\n+        # We only enable custom allreduce for MI300 series and gfx1250\r\n+        return any(gfx in _GCN_ARCH for gfx in [\"gfx94\", \"gfx95\", \"gfx1250\"])\r\n```\r\n\r\nNo other change is needed. `VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_CUSTOM_AR` already defaults to on, the IPC pool (`AiterCustomAllreduce.MAX_SIZE`) is unchanged, and no AITER environment variable is required. Other architectures are unaffected.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\nAll on gfx1250. The serving and accuracy runs used ROCm's gfx1250 development branch with the identical commit applied (same patch-id). \"Before\" is the same build without it.\r\n\r\n1. AITER's multi-GPU custom allreduce test at TP4 (`op_tests/multigpu_tests/test_custom_allreduce.py -t 4`): the regression suite, plus a size sweep under CUDA graphs.\r\n2. `vllm bench serve` on DeepSeek-V4-Pro (TP4) and DeepSeek-V4-Flash (TP2): random dataset, 8k/1k and 1k/1k tokens at concurrency 16 and 64, temperature 0, `--ignore-eos`. Each config runs twice; the tables show the second run.\r\n3. gsm8k on DeepSeek-V4-Pro: 5-shot, temperature 0, full test set, batch sizes 16 / 64 / 128.\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n**AITER custom allreduce, TP4, bf16:**\r\n\r\n- The tail regressions pass, eager and under CUDA graphs.\r\n- The sweep from 1K to 32M elements (64 MiB) matches the reference within bf16 rounding (max error about 2e-4).\r\n- Latency is 7.5 µs for small messages and 345 µs at 64 MiB.\r\n\r\n**DeepSeek-V4-Pro, TP4:**\r\n\r\n10/29 updates:\r\n| config | total tok/s | mean TTFT (ms) | median TTFT (ms) | mean TPOT (ms) |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| 8k/1k c16 | 5934 → 6704 (+13.0%) | 504 → 488 (−3.2%) | 486 → 466 | 23.79 → 21.02 (−11.6%) |\r\n| 8k/1k c64 | 16578 → 21659 (+30.6%) | 782 → 769 (−1.7%) | 704 → 699 | 33.99 → 25.85 (−23.9%) |\r\n| 1k/1k c16 | 1623 → 1846 (+13.8%) | 352 → 362 (+2.6%) | 354 → 365 | 19.40 → 17.00 (−12.4%) |\r\n| 1k/1k c64 | 4267 → 5729 (+34.3%) | 1124 → 1136 (+1.0%) | 1122 → 1135 | 28.92 → 21.25 (−26.5%) |\r\n\r\n**DeepSeek-V4-Flash, TP2:**\r\n\r\n| ISL / OSL, concurrency | total tok/s | mean TPOT (ms) | median TTFT (ms) |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| 8192 / 1024, 16 | 10543 → 11290 (+7.1%) | 13.15 → 12.38 (−5.9%) | 321 → 397 |\r\n| 8192 / 1024, 64 | 29202 → 33154 (+13.5%) | 19.11 → 16.66 (−12.8%) | 618 → 584 |\r\n| 1024 / 1024, 16 | 2577 → 2794 (+8.4%) | 12.12 → 11.16 (−7.9%) | 313 → 309 |\r\n| 1024 / 1024, 64 | 6887 → 8292 (+20.4%) | 17.70 → 14.78 (−16.5%) | 669 → 643 |\r\n\r\nTTFT varies run to run and moves in both directions, so the change is within noise.\r\n\r\n**gsm8k, DeepSeek-V4-Pro** (strict / flexible-extract):\r\n\r\n10/29 updates:\r\n| batch size | before | this PR |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| 16 | 0.9492 / 0.9484 | 0.9507 / 0.9500 |\r\n| 64 | 0.9447 / 0.9447 | 0.9553 / 0.9545 |\r\n| 128 | 0.9500 / 0.9492 | 0.9477 / 0.9477 |\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
